# Innovus write_stream layer map for sky130 with the sky130_fd_sc_hd tech LEF
# (sky130_fd_sc_hd__nom.tlef layer names).
#
# Columns: <LEF layer | NAME> <object types> <GDS layer> <GDS datatype(s)>
# GDS numbers are those of the PDK layermap
# ($SKY130/libs/sky130_fd_pr_main/sky130_fd_pr_main.layermap):
#   <layer> drawing = 20 (cut layers 44), pin = 16, label = 5, fill = 99.
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped, so they are not written at all:
#   DIEAREA      the die box (the 22 Sep stream had it on 129/0; 235/4 would
#                trip the deck's x.prBndry warning). The pad ring and corner
#                pads already span the die.
#   COMP         instance outlines (were 128/0) and NAME COMP instance-name
#                text (were 127/0).
#   LEFOBS/LEFPIN  only used with -output_macros, which stream_out.tcl does not
#                pass: every master comes from a -merge GDS instead.
#   NAME .../NET and .../SPNET  per-shape net-name text; LVS needs only the
#                top-level port labels (PIN below, TEXT from create_text).
#   nwell/pwell/licon  Innovus draws nothing on them at the top level.
#
# Comments must start with '#' as the first or last field of a line.

# ---- li1 (only via landings and pin access; not a routing layer here)
li1   NET,SPNET,VIA      67  20
li1   PIN                67  20,16
li1   FILL               67  99
li1   TEXT               67  5
NAME  li1/PIN            67  5
mcon  VIA,VIAFILL        67  44

# ---- met1
met1  NET,SPNET,VIA      68  20
met1  PIN                68  20,16
met1  FILL               68  99
met1  TEXT               68  5
NAME  met1/PIN           68  5
via   VIA,VIAFILL        68  44

# ---- met2
met2  NET,SPNET,VIA      69  20
met2  PIN                69  20,16
met2  FILL               69  99
met2  TEXT               69  5
NAME  met2/PIN           69  5
via2  VIA,VIAFILL        69  44

# ---- met3
met3  NET,SPNET,VIA      70  20
met3  PIN                70  20,16
met3  FILL               70  99
met3  TEXT               70  5
NAME  met3/PIN           70  5
via3  VIA,VIAFILL        70  44

# ---- met4
met4  NET,SPNET,VIA      71  20
met4  PIN                71  20,16
met4  FILL               71  99
met4  TEXT               71  5
NAME  met4/PIN           71  5
via4  VIA,VIAFILL        71  44

# ---- met5
met5  NET,SPNET,VIA      72  20
met5  PIN                72  20,16
met5  FILL               72  99
met5  TEXT               72  5
NAME  met5/PIN           72  5
